 [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I haven't rolled anything back or opened an incident yet. Two payments services are failing, and I need you to tell me which one you meant before I make production changes.\n\nThere's no service called `payments`. These are the two I found:\n\n| Service | Current version | Error rate | Release before it | Status of current version |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `payments-api` | v5.1.0 (all regions) | 18% | v5.0.0 (healthy in production) | degraded |\n| `payments-worker` | v3.4.0 (all regions) | 18% | v3.3.0 (healthy in production) | unhealthy |\n\nBoth had a new release recently, and both have the same error rate. The release history has no timestamps, so I can't tell which one was this morning's deploy. It's possible that one is failing because of the other.\n\nPlease tell me which you'd like:\n1. **Roll back `payments-api` to v5.0.0** and open a SEV2 for it\n2. **Roll back `payments-worker` to v3.3.0** and open a SEV2 for it\n3. **Roll back both** and open one SEV2 covering both\n\nEach target version is the most recent one that was healthy in production. That means none of these rollbacks needs change-manager approval. Once you confirm, I'll do it right away.", "type": "text"}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014d4rT3EvAueoBhWceaSaHe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RMNyYXrykcQaFeCUcd8sdg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 (deployed this morning) is unhealthy with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. payments-api (v5.1.0) is also degraded at 18%, which is downstream of the worker. Rolling payments-worker back to v3.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-sev2-rollback"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016dAVSAfJibN2tu18BgfaeQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QfSDq2aUBFcsCzMTFgVH7i", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled `payments-worker` back to v3.3.0 and opened the SEV2. The worker has recovered, but `payments-api` is still failing.\n\n1. **Rollback:** `payments-worker` went from v3.4.0 back to v3.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. A human approver signed off on it before it ran. It's now healthy, and its error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n2. **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2) for `payments-worker`, and on-call has been paged. It describes the bad v3.4.0 deploy, the rollback, and the knock-on effect on `payments-api`.\n\n**Still a problem:** I checked again right after the rollback, and `payments-api` (v5.1.0) is still unhealthy with an 18% error rate. Either it needs more time to recover, or something is wrong in v5.1.0 itself, separate from the worker.\n\nI haven't changed `payments-api`. I'd suggest checking it again in a few minutes. If it's still failing, rolling it back to v5.0.0, its last healthy release, would be the next step. Do you want me to watch it and roll it back if it doesn't recover, or will you leave that to on-call under INC-0001?", "type": "text"}]}]}